  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `site/config.toml`: `build_search_index = true` with a `[search]` block: `index_format = \"elasticlunr_javascript\"` (so the index is `search_index.en.js`), title, description and path indexed, body indexed truncated to 2000 characters.\n- `site/templates/base.html`: a search form in the header. It loads `vendor/elasticlunr.min.js` and `search_index.<default_language>.js` with `get_url`, then a small inline script. Results are a dropdown under the box, built with `textContent` (no `innerHTML`). Keyboard: Down from the box enters the results, Up/Down move between them, Enter follows the first result on submit, Escape closes and returns focus to the box. Result links are the URLs Zola builds from `base_url`, so the base path is carried and no host is hard-coded.\n- `site/static/vendor/elasticlunr.min.js` is elasticlunr 0.9.5 from the npm tarball, unmodified, with its MIT licence in `site/static/vendor/elasticlunr.LICENSE.txt`. No third-party service at run time.\n- `site/static/style.css`: search styles in the existing tokens (`--bg`, `--card`, `--line`, `--fg`, `--muted`, `--accent`), so the dropdown follows the dark theme; under 600px the box takes the full header row.\n- `site/README.md`: a short note on search and `vendor/`.\n- `docs/decisions/1245-site-search.md`: the decisions taken unattended.\n\nNo `.github/` change: the existing `zola build` in the `site` job picks up the config, so the maintainer does not need to touch the workflow.\n\n## How tested\n\n- Zola 0.23.6 (`brew install zola`, the version pinned in `release.yml`).\n- `zola build --base-url https://neotech.github.io/Camcraft` in `site/`: builds; `public/search_index.en.js` (195 KB) and `public/vendor/elasticlunr.min.js` exist; the index's document URLs use the Pages base path.\n- `zola serve --port 1111` (base_url `http://127.0.0.1:1111`): `GET /` and `/guide/setups/` include the search box and both script tags; `GET /vendor/elasticlunr.min.js` returns 200 (17827 bytes); `GET /search_index.en.js` returns 200 (175688 bytes) and its links use the local base.\n- Index queries run in Node against the built files (elasticlunr loaded from `vendor/`, the index from `search_index.en.js`, the same calls the inline script makes):\n  - `refused` → 7 hits (first: \"Reading a refusal\").\n  - `WCS` → 1 hit (\"Setups\").\n  - `adaptive` → 1 hit (\"Operations\").\n  - a nonsense term → 0 hits.\n\nNo Rust code changed, so no cargo gate was run.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The dropdown in a real browser: keyboard flow, focus and Escape behaviour, and the phone-width and dark-mode looks were not checked visually. The logic was checked only through the index queries above.\n- The Pages deploy itself; the `site` job's `zola build` with the release base URL was not run in CI.\n- Pages with no body text (their excerpt falls back to the description) were not reviewed one by one.\n\nChangelog: none (docs-only)\n\nFixes #1245\n",
